{
  "_comment": [
    "The fixed validation take for the Solo Violin voicebank. Every A/B claim",
    "about engine sound quality is made on THIS phrase, rendered before and",
    "after, so two files can be compared sample for sample.",
    "",
    "It is built to expose the specific failures the renderer has been prone to:",
    "  0-8 s    sustained tones at recorded and BETWEEN-recorded pitches, so",
    "           transposition artefacts and dynamic-layer blending are audible",
    "           on a held note rather than hidden under an attack.",
    "  8-16 s   legato steps with drawn pitch lines: scoops, a slow portamento,",
    "           and a vibrato written as data, which exercise continuous pitch.",
    "  16-24 s  short articulated notes, where a lost or clicking release shows.",
    "  24-40 s  one very long held note. A stateful renderer that drifts, grows",
    "           DC, or degrades over time only reveals it here.",
    "",
    "Durations deliberately outrun the ~2 s recorded samples so the loop and",
    "release paths are both entered on almost every note."
  ],
